---
ANNE OF GREEN GABLES
by L. M. Montgomery
"Marilla, isn't it nice to think that tomorrow 
is a new day with no \nmistakes in it yet?"
"I'll warrant you'll \nmake plenty in it,"
said Marilla.
"Yes, and well I know \nit," admitted Anne
mournfully. "But have \nyou ever noticed one
encouraging thing about me, Marilla? 
I never make the same \nmistake twice."
